command-code provides the Command Code coding agent CLI 1.93.4, installed
under tools/command-code/.

Launchers
  Linux/macOS: tools/command-code/cmd, cmdc, commandcode, command-code
  Windows:     tools/command-code\cmdc.cmd, command-code.cmd, commandcode.cmd
               (cmd.cmd is installed but Windows resolves the built-in cmd.exe first)

Run
  cmd --help
  cmd --version
  cmdc

The launcher keeps the current working directory as the agent workspace.

Runtime requirement
  Node.js 22+ is required. The launcher prefers Node from PATH and falls back
  to the nodejs22 host tool when the 'nodejs22' feature is enabled. If neither
  is usable it prints an error and exits with code 127.

License
  The upstream npm package declares "UNLICENSED" and ships no license text;
  this port records that in share/command-code/copyright (manifest license is
  null). Review the upstream terms before redistribution.

Conditional nodejs22 dependency
  The manifest declares a 'nodejs22' feature whose dependency is the standalone
  host tool port nodejs22. Use the provided install.sh / install.ps1 script: it
  checks the system Node first and enables the feature only when no usable
  Node is present, so vcpkg installs nodejs22 exactly in that case.
  Example: ./install.sh --vcpkg-root /path/to/vcpkg --triplet x64-linux
  The dependency is visible with:
    vcpkg depend-info 'command-code[nodejs22]' --overlay-ports=... --format=tree
